  "interpretation": [
    "All 22 regular Hunodan browser workflows remain below ten seconds on this machine, with byte-identical exported geometry and editable SVGs. Median 6.3585 seconds, maximum 9.221 seconds; prior release was 5.7611 and 8.8593. This is not a universal speedup.",
    "All 55 native replays retain their counts and candidate pass/fail decisions. Seven observed-image errors decrease, twelve increase and thirty-six remain equal. The largest increase is 0.080625 percentage points, not hidden by aggregate pass counts.",
    "The half-resolution puppy browser solve falls from 20.499 to 13.2065 seconds; its editable source disagreement rises slightly from 1.190664 to 1.193951 percent. The native replay instead improves slightly. Time-limited refinement prevents an exact invariance or universal quality claim.",
    "The new initial-geometry preference is recorded for the two puppy cases and the bauble. No Hunodan case uses it. Other changed photo outputs are not causally attributed from this single timed comparison.",
    "The clipped-photo browser workflow preserves the original observed region through upload, rough selection, edit/undo/redo, solving and editable SVG export. Its observed editable disagreement is 0.5375626 percent.",
    "This cycle validates fixed masks and selected real browser workflows. It does not add raw-photo successes to the separate 31-photo benchmark, admit neural labels, or establish original template recovery/physical assembly. The outlined-star feature and bauble fidelity failures remain."
  ],
